<article class="env-lemma" id="0H5F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H5F">Lemma <span data-tag="0H5F">62.6.15</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $X$ be a scheme locally of finite type over $S$. Let $r \geq 0$. Let $U \subset X$ be an open such that $X \setminus U$ has relative dimension $< r$ over $S$, i.e., $\dim (X_ s \setminus U_ s) < r$ for all $s \in S$. Then restriction defines a bijection $z(X/S, r) \to z(U/S, r)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $Z_ r(X_ s) \to Z_ r(U_ s)$ is a bijection by the dimension assumption, we see that restriction induces a bijection between families of $r$-cycles on the fibres of $X/S$ and families of $r$-cycles on the fibres of $U/S$. These restriction maps $Z_ r(X_ s) \to Z_ r(U_ s)$ are compatible with base change and with specializations, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0H4P" data-tag="0H4P">62.5.1</a> and <a href="/tag/0H4L" data-tag="0H4L">62.4.4</a>. The lemma follows easily from this; details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>